[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="AttributionEntry" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://attribution/attribution_entry.gd" id="1_entry"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_entry")
id = "quaternius_farm_buildings"
creator = "Quaternius"
source_name = "Farm Buildings"
source_version = "September 2018"
creator_url = "https://quaternius.com"
source_url = "https://quaternius.com"
support_url = "https://www.patreon.com/quaternius"
license_name = "CC0 1.0 Universal (CC0 1.0) Public Domain Dedication"
license_url = "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"
license_file = "res://assets/licenses/Quaternius_UltimateAnimatedAnimals_License.txt"
attribution_required = false
required_notice = ""
conditions = ""
assets_used = PackedStringArray("Barn", "SmallBarn", "OpenBarn", "ChickenCoop", "Silo", "Windmill", "WaterTower", "Well")
per_file_licensing = false
notes = "CC0 — crediting is courtesy, not compliance. FIRST use of this pack in the project
(2026-08-26, content-variety pass Task 3) — no prior entry existed, so this is a new
AttributionEntry rather than an extension, per asset-import-pipeline.md's \"same source
pack as an existing entry\" vs. \"new source\" distinction.

Pack ships its own License.txt at `source-content/assets/Farm Buildings - Sept 2018.../
License.txt`, re-checked before import per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate —
confirmed CC0 1.0 Universal / Public Domain Dedication, same generic Quaternius CC0
boilerplate already preserved as license_file for the Ultimate Animated Animal Pack (not
pack-specific text) — reused rather than duplicated, same convention as every other
Quaternius entry in this project.

TEXTURE AUDIT FINDING, recorded here as well as per-scene (see each Barn.tscn-sibling
header): at plan time no texture files were found anywhere in this pack's extracted
folder (only a Preview.png) — this was correctly treated as a LEAD, not a conclusion, and
empirically verified via a throwaway probe script (same method used to diagnose the
DeadTree/PineTree2 missing-texture bug earlier this session). Result: this pack never
shipped textures at all, in ANY of its export formats (confirmed by inspecting the
sibling OBJ/MTL export's .mtl files directly — no `map_Kd` line anywhere) — it instead
bakes each of its named flat-color Blender materials (DarkRed, LightRed, RoofBlack,
White, Brown, Grey, Black, DarkGrey, etc.) into real per-vertex color at FBX export time.
Every one of the 8 imported buildings was probed individually and shows MEANINGFUL,
DISTINCT per-surface vertex colors, not the uniform near-(0.9063, 0.9063, 0.9063, 1.0)
missing-texture tell that flagged DeadTree/PineTree2 as broken. No texture fix was
needed for any of the 8; no material_override was applied anywhere in this pack's
wrapper scenes.

Per-asset destination and use (all 8, first use of each):
  - Barn.fbx -> project/assets/buildings/barn/Barn.fbx -> Barn.tscn ->
    project/data/buildings/barn.tres (proposed 2x2 footprint, the one outlier in this
    batch's cost/footprint table — see barn.tres's own header).
  - SmallBarn.fbx -> project/assets/buildings/small_barn/SmallBarn.fbx ->
    SmallBarn.tscn -> project/data/buildings/small_barn.tres.
  - OpenBarn.fbx -> project/assets/buildings/open_barn/OpenBarn.fbx -> OpenBarn.tscn ->
    project/data/buildings/open_barn.tres.
  - ChickenCoop.fbx -> project/assets/buildings/chicken_coop/ChickenCoop.fbx ->
    ChickenCoop.tscn -> project/data/buildings/chicken_coop.tres.
  - Silo.fbx -> project/assets/buildings/silo/Silo.fbx -> Silo.tscn ->
    project/data/buildings/silo.tres.
  - Windmill.fbx -> project/assets/buildings/windmill/Windmill.fbx -> Windmill.tscn ->
    project/data/buildings/windmill.tres (this pack also ships a taller
    TowerWindmill.fbx, not used here — Windmill.fbx is what this task's proposal table
    specifies).
  - WaterTower.fbx -> project/assets/buildings/water_tower/WaterTower.fbx ->
    WaterTower.tscn -> project/data/buildings/water_tower.tres.
  - Well.fbx -> project/assets/buildings/well/Well.fbx -> Well.tscn ->
    project/data/buildings/well.tres.

The pack ships more buildings beyond these 8 (BigBarn, Silo_House, Fence, Fence2,
TowerWindmill) plus Blend/OBJ source formats not used here; append to assets_used as any
more are imported, do NOT create a second entry for this pack."
